  "overview": {
    "text": "Frequency describes how often a repeating event occurs: it is the number of cycles or oscillations completed—or waves passing a fixed point—per unit time. It is a core way to characterize periodic motion and waves, alongside period, amplitude, and (for waves) wavelength. If one cycle takes period T, frequency f = 1/T, so a faster repetition has a shorter period. Frequency is measured in hertz (Hz), with 1 Hz equal to one cycle per second. For a traveling wave, speed v equals frequency times wavelength (v = fλ); when wave speed in a medium is fixed, higher frequency corresponds to shorter wavelength. In sound, higher frequency is heard as higher pitch.",
    "source_urls": [
      "https://openstax.org/books/physics/pages/5-5-simple-harmonic-motion",
      "https://openstax.org/books/physics/pages/13-2-wave-properties-speed-amplitude-frequency-and-period",
      "https://www.nist.gov/pml/owm/si-units-time"
    ]
  },
  "key_facts": [
    {
      "text": "For repeating motion, the period is the time taken for one complete oscillation; frequency counts oscillations per unit time.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://openstax.org/books/physics/pages/5-5-simple-harmonic-motion"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Frequency and period are reciprocals: f = 1/T. A shorter period means a higher frequency.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://openstax.org/books/physics/pages/5-5-simple-harmonic-motion",
        "https://openstax.org/books/physics/pages/13-2-wave-properties-speed-amplitude-frequency-and-period"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The hertz (Hz) is the SI unit of frequency; 1 Hz equals one cycle per second.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://www.nist.gov/pml/owm/si-units-time"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For a traveling wave, v = fλ; at a fixed wave speed, increasing frequency means decreasing wavelength.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://openstax.org/books/physics/pages/13-2-wave-properties-speed-amplitude-frequency-and-period"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For sound, higher frequency corresponds to higher pitch.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://openstax.org/books/physics/pages/13-2-wave-properties-speed-amplitude-frequency-and-period"
      ]
    }
  ],
